# Citation File Format v1.2
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button on the project page when this
# file is present. Update `version` / `date-released` on every tagged release,
# and fill in the `preferred-citation` doi / journal fields once the paper is
# accepted.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: slicedcommittor
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the article and the software
  itself, using the metadata in `preferred-citation` below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Petersen
    given-names: Magnus
    affiliation: >-
      Goethe University Frankfurt and Frankfurt Institute for Advanced Studies,
      Frankfurt am Main, Germany
    email: mapetersen@fias.uni-frankfurt.de
  - family-names: Lichtinger
    given-names: Simon
    affiliation: >-
      Goethe University Frankfurt and Frankfurt Institute for Advanced Studies,
      Frankfurt am Main, Germany
  - family-names: Covino
    given-names: Roberto
    affiliation: >-
      Goethe University Frankfurt and Frankfurt Institute for Advanced Studies,
      Frankfurt am Main, Germany
repository-code: "https://github.com/MagnusPetersen/slicedcommittor"
url: "https://github.com/MagnusPetersen/slicedcommittor"
abstract: >-
  Sample-based committor approximation via random 1D projections.
  The library writes the committor as a weighted sum of 1D
  reaction-diffusion committors along random projections, with weights
  recovered from a single symmetric linear solve on equilibrium samples,
  at cost linear in the number of samples and the configuration-space
  dimension.
keywords:
  - committor
  - reaction-rate
  - rare-events
  - molecular-dynamics
  - transition-path-theory
  - sliced-methods
  - jax
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"

